WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.230
Speaker 1: Mike Pence is running for president,
one of the most electric and inspiring candidates.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.920
No, that's not true.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.889
That's actually very much untrue.

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:15.360
Mike Pence, this is a weird 2024 Republican
primary already.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.870
Mike Pence also spoke at the Iowa Roast and
Ride.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:27.500
And it is actually stunning how Mike Pence
is embroiled in a battle with Ron DeSantis

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.910
for who could possibly be the least charismatic
candidate so far.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:37.450
Here is Pence in a speech no one understood
nor cared about.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:49.300
Speaker 2: It is great to be back at the roast
and ride I rode and I roasted on the ride.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.219
Speaker 1: Wow.

00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:56.070
Just absolutely electric delivery, as you
can see there.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.070
Pence seemingly out of ideas.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:02.300
He sort of, you know how on gun violence it's
like we've tried nothing and we're all out

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.830
of ideas is very often what you hear from
some on the right.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:12.470
Pence so far has really tried nothing to justify
his candidacy, and he's just doing a little

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:16.869
bit of the DeSantis stuff, talking about Bud
Light and, you know, Target.

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:21.360
I don't think that this is if DeSantis can't
win with this stuff.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.079
I don't know that Pence can win with the exact
same stuff.

00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:26.460
Speaker 2: He also has to stand up for American
families.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.460
Okay.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.430
You know, the truth of the matter is we stand
here today.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:35.950
Now, the radical left has been assaulting
our values and assaulting our families almost

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.200
as never before.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.890
Speaker 1: Well, talk to me about how that's
going to get me a better paying job or more

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:41.890
job security, Mike.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:42.890
Oh, right.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:43.890
It won't.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:44.950
It's the same nonsense DeSantis is peddling.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:50.540
Speaker 2: But the great thing I've seen traveling
across this country is that the American people,

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.680
American people are onto.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.060
Are they?

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:56.330
Just ask Bud Light.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:59.049
Target.

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:03.310
And by the way, a message from Major League
Baseball.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:07.710
Religious bigotry has no place in America's
pastime.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:15.790
Speaker 1: You can tell he really means it
because he's moving his hands.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:19.950
Oh.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:20.950
All right.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.180
And pens pointing to someone into the crowd
and mouthing, Thank you.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:31.770
As you can see, this campaign does not exactly
have victory written all over it.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:35.450
Here is Mike Pence interviewed there right
before, right after this thing.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.110
He's wearing some kind of biker vest.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:41.130
It might be leather, it might be pleather.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:45.700
And asked about his big announcement, which
is scheduled for tomorrow.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:52.489
And if anybody was worried that Mike Pence's
announcement might not be blessed by God,

00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:54.150
he has been praying about it.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.150
He notifies us.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:58.750
Speaker 2: Right 50 miles into the state fairgrounds.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.810
If that doesn't say I'm running for president,
I don't know what is.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.239
Are you ready to make it official?

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:07.069
Well, we're looking forward to be back in
Iowa next Wednesday.

00:03:07.069 --> 00:03:08.069
Yeah.

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:11.580
Now, Karen and I spent a lot of time over
the last two years reflecting and frankly

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.459
praying about where we make.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:20.440
Speaker 1: The same God that told George W
Bush to go into Iraq when he prayed.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.320
Is apparently advising the Pence's.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.799
Speaker 2: Next serve our country after our
years in Congress or years as governor of

00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:27.930
Indiana and years as vice president.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.239
We've come to a decision.

00:03:29.239 --> 00:03:33.810
I thought there'd be no better place to announce
our decision than right here in the Hawkeye

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:34.810
State.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.810
Well, let me ask is right.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.459
Speaker 1: Super, super exciting, as you can
see.

00:03:37.459 --> 00:03:40.330
So, listen, how how is Mike?

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.879
But what is Mike Pence doing?

00:03:41.879 --> 00:03:43.819
How is Mike Pence doing in this race?

00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:47.739
The latest polling has Mike Pence at an anemic
3.8%.

00:03:47.739 --> 00:03:55.250
I'll be honest, I don't even know how Mike
Pence has a path to getting ahead of Ron DeSantis.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.790
Never mind catching Donald Trump.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:01.630
I don't understand Mike Pence's argument for
even being a candidate.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.489
If you didn't like the Trump administration.

00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:07.019
Pence was part of that administration.

00:04:07.019 --> 00:04:13.090
If you did like the Trump administration,
Trump's running and you can vote for Trump.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:19.079
And if you didn't like Trump, but you want
someone with a viable path to victory, you've

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:20.769
got Ron DeSantis.

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:25.830
If you want a woman representing the Republican
Party, you've got Nikki Haley.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:30.650
If you want a black guy representing the Republican
Party, you've got Tim Scott.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:35.720
If you want a guy who's good at debating,
representing the Republican Party, you've

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.060
got Chris Christie.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.710
I don't know what path there is for this guy.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:44.009
And it makes me wonder why is he running at
all?

00:04:44.009 --> 00:04:46.480
I haven't heard him justify it in any way.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.650
That makes sense.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.650
Maybe somebody in the audience has a clue.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:50.650
Let me know.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:56.470
Make sure you subscribe to the YouTube channel
YouTube.com, slash the David Pacman show.

